 34CL    33S(3HE,D)                    2014PA44,1971ER03         ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+33}S+1p|){+34}Cl from J|p=3/2+ {+33}S ground state.                  
 34CL c  2014Pa44: a 25-MeV {+3}He beam was provided from the 14-MV MP tandem   
 34CL2c  accelerator at the Maier-Leibnitz Laboratory, Garching, Germany.       
 34CL3c  Targets were Ag{+2}{+33}S (20 |mg/cm{+2}, enriched to 99.9% {+33}S)    
 34CL4c  deposited upon a foil of {+12}C; Ag{+2}S (20 |mg/cm{+2}, natural       
 34CL5c  sulphur) deposited upon a foil of {+12}C; a 50 |mg/cm{+2} Ag foil; a 7 
 34CL6c  |mg/cm{+2} {+12}C foil; and {+24}Mg (20 |mg/cm{+2}, enriched to 99.92% 
 34CL7c  {+24}Mg) deposited upon a foil of {+12}C. All {+12}C foils were        
 34CL8c  enriched to 99.99% and of thickness 7 |mg/cm{+2}. Light reaction       
 34CL9c  products were momentum-analyzed by the Q3D magnetic spectrograph and   
 34CLAc  detected in the focal plane using a a multiwire gas-filled proportional
 34CLBc  counter backed by a plastic scintillator at FWHM=12 keV. Measured      
 34CLCc  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and spectroscopic    
 34CLDc  factors from FRESCO-DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q). Also deduced 
 34CLEc  resonance strengths and the thermonuclear {+33}S(p,|g){+34}Cl reaction 
 34CLFc  rate. Calculated {+32}S/{+33}S ratios in the composition of nova ejecta
 34CLGc  via hydrodynamic nova simulations.                                     
 34CL c  1971Er03: a 14-MeV {+3}He beam was provided from the Argonne tandem Van
 34CL2c  de Graaff accelerator. Targets were CdS on C backing, enriched to 83%  
 34CL3c  in {+33}S. Deuterons were detected using nuclear track emulsions in the
 34CL4c  focal plane of the Enge split-pole magnetic spectrograph with an energy
 34CL5c  resolution of 17 keV. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels,           
 34CL6c  L-transfers, J, |p, and spectroscopic factors from JULIE-DWBA analysis 
 34CL7c  of the measured |s(|q).                                                
 34CL cL S$LABEL=[(2J{-f}+1)/(2J{-i}+1)]C{+2}S                                  
 34CL cL E$For levels below 4.64 MeV, from 1971Er03; for levels above 4.64 MeV, 
 34CL2cL from 2014Pa44, unless otherwise noted.                                 
 34CL cL E(A)$Rounded from the Adopted Levels without uncertainties. 2014Pa44   
 34CL2cL observed these levels and used the E(level) values from the Adopted    
 34CL3cL Levels of 2012Ni10 for calibration.                                    
 34CL cL L,S$From DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q) in 1971Er03 (below 4.63  
 34CL2cL MeV) and 2014Pa44 (above 4.63 MeV). The spectroscopic factors C{+2}S   
 34CL3cL given by 1971Er03 are defined as [(2J{-f}+1)/(2J{-i}+1)]C{+2}S, where  
 34CL4cL C{+2}=1/2 is the isospin coefficient, J{-f} and J{-i}, are the final   
 34CL5cL and initial spins, respectively. J{-i}=3/2 for {+33}S ground state.    
